WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.800
I think part of the, really
important part of the process

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.580
of package lifecycle
and package development

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.380
is not just adding
new functions,

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.380
but it is equally important
to remove those functions.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.100
And we know that removing
functions that used to work

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.000
is frustrating.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.920
And so we have developed this
process, this lifecycle process

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.000
of deprecation where it starts
with pretty mild warnings

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.100
and gets progressively
aggressive, more

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.420
and more aggressive over time.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.160
We hope this is useful.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.400
We hope that this
gradually pushes

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.960
you towards the golden
path without forcing you rudely

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.280
when you're working
on something else

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.080
to urgently switch something.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.320
But at the same time,
we believe that we want

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.520
these functions to be better.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.040
We want these things to
have a more consistent,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.720
cohesive syntax
because that makes

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.340
it easier for future users.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.100
And I think we're
doing pretty well.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.320
We've certainly
got a lot better,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.780
I think, at handling
deprecation and breakages,

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:06.840
but we're certainly still
trying, still learning.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.300
And if you have any
feedback, please let us know.

